# Derived by hand from Type System ch. 5 (a `u fn` takes its color from its call; the function the event holds is the one passed) and Semantics ch. 3 (`on` fires with its left side's value in the tick of its event; a function lifted over an event fires in that tick): the click fires the function, which adds one to 5. Never run.
test it_fires

